WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:11.100
At Worlds end a young woman clutches an egg, fully devoted, to protecting, whatever's inside

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:18.480
Alas, she's approached by a warrior who crushes the egg shattering all of the illusions that it represented I

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.189
I could just as easily be talking about Dark Souls 3 with that statement

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:29.840
fact is Miyazaki has a long-standing tradition of pulling quite heavily from other forms of Media

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.420
And just like learning about Artorias from Guts

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.410
just like learning about Bloodborne from HP Lovecraft

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:44.080
I want Angel's egg to teach us about Filianore and I will answer the following questions:

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.320
One, what does the egg represent?

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:53.300
And two, how does Filianore have the power to forestall the end of the world?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.560
And make no mistake, that's exactly what she's doing.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.500
These questions aren't really touched upon in the game at all.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.560
Not in any descriptions, and you'd think that they would be

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:09.740
But Angel's egg, this animated movie made by Mamoru Oshii in 1985

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:15.400
succinctly answers both of these questions, and the answer is faith

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:23.489
A young girl wonders an abandoned City filling glass urns with water she knows not why she does this yet

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:28.439
She does it all the same and in much the same way she carries and protect this large egg

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:31.079
holding it closely throughout the movie

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:34.739
And long story short you should watch the movie if you're interested

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:42.180
one of the very few pieces of dialogue in this movie talks about a bird that represents life outside of this world

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.520
and the girl believes that the bird now resides inside of the egg.

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:12.140
This character, the warrior wishes to break the egg and know one way or another

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:15.840
what's inside. But the girl believes it will hatch.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.940
And the point I want to make is this:

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:21.960
Blind faith offers this great deal of power ,because

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:28.860
Believing something will hatch from the egg many would say is better than knowing one way or another

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:34.760
For there may well be nothing inside the egg or whatever's inside might have already died

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:38.320
So compared to the grim skeptical warrior

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:45.039
The girl is comforted by her faith, and she moves with purpose. She's protected by Faith

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:09.059
The end result of analyzing Angel's egg in this way is that we can now

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:12.719
reliably ascribe Faith to Filianore's character

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.029
And that's very important because in Dark souls faith has a remarkable amount of power

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:25.769
I mean think about it when you learn a miracle in this game what you're actually doing from a lore perspective is learning how to

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:33.989
Recite the words of a famous miracle the mere act of which can heal wounds emit Force cast lightning

00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:36.370
many other things

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:42.120
"Miracles began as tales told by gods passed down through us since the first flame"

00:03:42.579 --> 00:03:47.549
"Isn't it extraordinary to think they've existed since the very origins of the world"

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:54.390
Furthermore true faith is blind that much is obvious and it's at the very core of faith

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:59.099
But in Dark souls 3 it takes that a little bit further because not only do miracles

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.700
Require Faith it just so happens that being blind

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.680
enhances their power

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:08.009
Remember all tomes in Dark Souls 3 are actually in Braille

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:12.380
which is a language of physical bumps for the blind to be able to read

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:18.620
A practice in Dark Souls 3 that is informed from the tradition of placing and I quote,

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.040
great faith in the words of the blind.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.640
So not only is Filianore a blind woman of faith

00:04:24.789 --> 00:04:30.269
She's also the daughter of Gwyn, and she doesn't need to recite no simple miracle

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:32.880
It's likely that she is the miracle

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:39.140
This legendary character, a direct descendant of what could only be called a God,

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.820
Is something you tell tales about

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:48.399
So she has power we know that much, but what is this power being put towards

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:53.360
I think there is only really one possible answer which is this,

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.080
Filianore prevents time from passing, we know this because,

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.220
Disturbing her doesn't just dispel a simple illusion

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:07.820
It actually brings us forward in time to the Ringed City which has fallen to ash

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:11.860
To Gael, with his rusted and broken weapons in hand

00:05:12.409 --> 00:05:17.259
to the Pygmy lords the blood of the dark soul dried in their veins and

00:05:17.959 --> 00:05:25.149
Back to Filianore, dead and withered perhaps at the moment where her faith or her power

00:05:25.849 --> 00:05:28.748
Finally gave out, so we've done our best to

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:37.179
Establish the power by which Filianore holds back time, but what is she manipulating? What does she have control over with this power?

00:05:37.789 --> 00:05:42.338
Well, it's possible that she's manipulating light because light

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:44.479
equals time

00:05:44.479 --> 00:05:48.428
according to the repair Sorcery which assumedly uses light to

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:54.940
Reverse time upon your weapons, the foundations of this spell are a well guarded secret,

00:05:55.260 --> 00:06:00.440
for light is time and the reversal of its effects is a forbidden art.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:06.320
If Filianore is indeed manipulating light to keep the Ringed City locked in time

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:09.400
Then you can kind of understand why this Magic would be both

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:16.020
forbidden and a well guarded secret, the gods would not want this power nor this

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:18.420
secret being used elsewhere

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:21.580
Light sorceries like repair which we just mentioned

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:24.480
hail from the Lost land of Oolacile

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:28.060
Which must have existed when the Ringed City was still in its prime,

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.900
because the two cities are connected by two characters

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:35.080
Who appeared who have moved from one to the other

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:40.600
two characters Halflight and Manus, let's talk about Halflight

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:44.480
A missionary is someone who is sent on a religious mission

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:51.320
and Halflight was one such missionary sent from an ancient land of sorcery which was obviously Oolacile

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:54.960
But he elected to stay behind in the Ringed City

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:58.400
Becoming the last recorded spear of the church

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:02.760
So this must have been before the two cities encountered hardship

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:07.940
And the two cities, when we visit them anyway, definitely are overrun

00:07:08.340 --> 00:07:11.200
As for the second character linking the two places together,

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:16.720
I want to convince you that Manus is at least a pygmy and

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:21.080
Potentially even the furtive pygmy may be from the Ringed City

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.080
The locust says this:

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:29.500
"One met the Dark with learning, but in the end learned his knowledge was wanting.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:34.560
The world began without knowledge, and without knowledge will it end."

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:40.660
And according to the white Birch bow description before its description was changed in a patch

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:47.780
it used to read "The bow is a relic from the land of an old sorcerer who was swallowed by the abyss

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:52.080
and known for his role in the heroic tale of the Abysswalker"

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:56.980
The only possible character known for his role in the tale of the Abysswalker'

00:07:56.980 --> 00:08:03.840
Who could possibly be an old Sorcerer, is Manus, which lines up with the fact that his weapon is indeed a catalyst

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:09.840
Thus Manus, who is called primeval man by Kaathe is three things at once

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:13.770
Manus is he who met the dark with knowledge when the world began

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.090
Manus is an old sorcerer who was swallowed by the abyss

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:24.640
And Manus most importantly is primeval man also known as a pygmy Lord

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:30.280
There's a story here, but we can only imagine it. It's a story of how a pygmy lord

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.140
left the Ringed City and settled in Oolacile

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:36.800
and eventually spread his abyss to the outside world.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:42.820
I'm going to quickfire a few other curiosities that I've found and you can follow these up in the description.

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:48.300
First, Ludleth may actually be a pygmy in the literal sense

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:53.900
This may well be something that the Japanese community has known for a long time because the line

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:57.740
"I may be small but I will die a colossus"

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:04.140
More literally translates to in Japanese "Even this pygmy here was honored to become a lord"

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:12.560
This raises interesting implications when you consider that Ludleth was exiled for the forbidden art of soul transposition

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:16.900
And consider also that Filianore's vagrant like shell

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:21.760
clearly contains a transposing kiln in the design works concept art.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:28.260
So could the Ringed City in fact be Courland and was Ludleth exiled from there?

00:09:28.260 --> 00:09:32.780
Reddit user Westby has a great little thread that goes into more detail

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:37.240
and in a point raised by Machi who's one of our new resident translators

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:41.560
Ludleth being a pygmy around since the very dawn of the world

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:47.120
certainly explains how he would have knowledge of the first Fire keeper, whoever she might have been.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:52.840
Because the eyes that we find in the untended graves are the eyes of the first Fire keeper

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:57.960
and Ludleth has dialogue about them saying that they reveal a frightful betrayal

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:04.780
and that they reveal a light that was lost by all fire keepers to come after this fire keeper

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:09.709
I've read that some have put forward that Filianore was the first fire keeper

00:10:09.709 --> 00:10:16.099
And I can see that, she is blind, she's presumably missing eyes and like a fire keeper

00:10:16.100 --> 00:10:21.300
she hold the darkness within her because darkness seeps from where her eye should be

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:28.100
and if Ludleth is indeed from here, then he should know of her. So that lines up pretty well

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:31.500
But all that said I'm not completely convinced about that

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:35.720
I mean the eyes are found on the corpse of another fire keeper

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:39.440
And while I supposed that they could be passed down from Filianore,

00:10:39.440 --> 00:10:44.860
should Filianore's eyes really reveal such a generic ending of the fire?

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:52.480
The world we see in Filianore's future is more of an end of the world not just the end of light

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:58.209
So as you might have gathered souls may well be over, but we're not done here

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:05.019
Also before I go. I am probably going to be in Japan by the time you see this video. Which is amazing

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:09.220
So I'm actually going to do a little travel blog or at least try to

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.390
About everywhere I've been, or the food I've eaten and all that sort of thing

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:20.000
So if you're interested into more of a window into my life, which I know is pretty Sparse on this channel

00:11:20.019 --> 00:11:22.179
Then I'm just going to do this for Patrons

00:11:22.180 --> 00:11:26.289
so if you want to consider becoming one of them you'll be doing that on behalf of

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:29.259
everyone who watches my videos and you get to see a little bit of

00:11:29.480 --> 00:11:32.260
what I'm going to be doing in Japan if that's interesting to you

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:38.740
it'll give me something to do while the other side of my mind is like crying that I'm not making videos and

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:45.279
Yeah, I kind of need to be creating something to make that anxiety go away, but thank you regardless

00:11:45.709 --> 00:11:51.489
Thank you for watching and thank you for being the 1% listening at the end of the video and I'll see you next time

